# NativeAOT and trimming

AuraORM is used from NativeAOT applications. The runtime library and every line the source generator emits must work there exactly as under the JIT.

- `src/AuraORM` is `IsAotCompatible`. The trim, AOT, and single-file analyzers run in every build, and their warnings are errors.
- No reflection that the trimmer cannot see: `Type.GetType(string)`, `Activator.CreateInstance(Type)`, `MakeGenericType`, `MakeGenericMethod`, `GetMethod` / `GetProperty` by name, `System.Reflection.Emit`, `Expression.Compile`. No expression trees at all (`System.Linq.Expressions` is banned): queries are built from typed expression objects, not from lambdas that are inspected. Mapping code that needs a per-type table is emitted by the source generator.
- No `[DynamicallyAccessedMembers]`, `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]`, `[RequiresDynamicCode]`, or `[UnconditionalSuppressMessage]` to silence an analyzer. If one seems needed, the design is wrong for AOT; raise it on the Issue.
- Per-type data is a `static class Cache<T>` field filled by generated code or a static constructor without reflection, never a `Dictionary<Type, ...>` filled at run time from reflection.
- The source generator ships inside the `AuraORM` package (`analyzers/dotnet/cs`), not as a separate package.
- Generic virtual methods and generic interfaces instantiated over many value types grow the binary. When one is added on a public type, the PR reports the size of the NativeAOT sample before and after.

## The check

CI publishes the NativeAOT sample (`samples/AuraORM.Samples.Sqlite`) for every PR on Linux and Windows, with `-warnaserror`, and runs it against SQLite. A row that adds public API exercises it in the sample. The job fails on any trim or AOT warning and on a failed run. A PR that changes the public surface, a dependency, or generated code reports the warning count (zero) and the executable size under `## Verification`.

Locally:

```powershell
$env:PATH += ';C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Installer'
dotnet publish samples/<Sample> -c Release -r win-x64 -o <scratch>
<scratch>/<Sample>.exe
```

A size that grew is split by what added it before the PR says so: publish with `-p:IlcGenerateMapFile=true` and compare the map files.
